        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Ogallala, Nebraska; Keith County; Nebraska; United States; Great Plains; Texas High Plains\n- Systems: Ogallala Aquifer\n- Topics: irrigation; vineyards\n\nFacts:\n- Ogallala is a city in Keith County, Nebraska, United States.\n- The Ogallala Aquifer is a shallow water table aquifer beneath the Great Plains in the United States, surrounded by sand, silt, clay, and gravel.\n- The Texas High Plains can be extremely dry, so most vineyards there are irrigated with water from the Ogallala Aquifer.",
